{
  "about": [
    "The reading view's parity corpus: one case list for both markdown renderers — the client's (web-ui/src/lib/previews/doc/, run by doc/parity.test.ts through its string target) and the daemon's comrak + ammonia fallback (crates/chimaera-server/src/fs.rs markdown_parity_tests). A case added here runs on both sides.",
    "md — the document. html — the expected body HTML (frontmatter is never body), compared after the shared normalization: lowercase tags; only the href, src, alt, id, class, align, start and data-task attributes, sorted; entities decoded and re-escaped one way; ASCII whitespace collapsed and dropped beside block tags; comments removed. data-sourcepos is dropped by that rule.",
    "diverges — set on a case the two sides are KNOWN to disagree on: `side` names the renderer that is skipped (the other must match `html`), `reason` says why. Fix a divergence on the client wherever feasible instead of adding one."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "note": "a plain paragraph",
      "md": "Hello world.\n",
      "html": "<p>Hello world.</p>"
    },
    {
      "note": "two paragraphs",
      "md": "One.\n\nTwo.\n",
      "html": "<p>One.</p><p>Two.</p>"
    },
    {
      "note": "a soft break flows",
      "md": "first line\nsecond line\n",
      "html": "<p>first line second line</p>"
    },
    {
      "note": "a hard break from two spaces",
      "md": "first  \nsecond\n",
      "html": "<p>first<br>second</p>"
    },
    {
      "note": "a hard break from a backslash",
      "md": "first\\\nsecond\n",
      "html": "<p>first<br>second</p>"
    },
    {
      "note": "trailing spaces at the paragraph end are no break",
      "md": "last line  \n",
      "html": "<p>last line</p>"
    },
    {
      "note": "backslash escapes",
      "md": "\\*not em\\* \\_ \\# \\[x\\] \\\\\n",
      "html": "<p>*not em* _ # [x] \\</p>"
    },
    {
      "note": "entities decode",
      "md": "&amp; &copy; &#35; &#x41; &lt;tag&gt; &hellip;\n",
      "html": "<p>&amp; © # A &lt;tag&gt; …</p>"
    },
    {
      "note": "an unknown entity stays literal",
      "md": "a &nosuch; b\n",
      "html": "<p>a &amp;nosuch; b</p>"
    },
    {
      "note": "emphasis and strong",
      "md": "*a* _b_ **c** __d__ ***e***\n",
      "html": "<p><em>a</em> <em>b</em> <strong>c</strong> <strong>d</strong> <em><strong>e</strong></em></p>"
    },
    {
      "note": "nested emphasis",
      "md": "**bold *and em* inside**\n",
      "html": "<p><strong>bold <em>and em</em> inside</strong></p>"
    },
    {
      "note": "intraword underscores stay literal",
      "md": "snake_case_word and a*b*c\n",
      "html": "<p>snake_case_word and a<em>b</em>c</p>"
    },
    {
      "note": "double-tilde strikethrough",
      "md": "~~gone~~ here\n",
      "html": "<p><del>gone</del> here</p>"
    },
    {
      "note": "single-tilde strikethrough",
      "md": "~gone~ here\n",
      "html": "<p><del>gone</del> here</p>"
    },
    {
